-The default retry policy doubles the delay until it reaches a fixed ceiling.
+The default retry policy grows linearly until it reaches a fixed ceiling.
+With a 100ms base, delays start at 100, 200, 300ms rather than 100, 200, 400ms.
+Faster later attempts shorten recovery waits but increase traffic during outages.
+Scheduler accepts a third argument mapping operation names to policy overrides.
+Pass the operation name as enqueue's third argument; unknown names are rejected.
+An exponential override suits downstream services that need more outage relief.
+Policies are resolved and copied at construction, so caller edits cannot change
+queued work. Attempt limits and transient-error eligibility retain their meaning.
 
